{
  "info": {
    "name": "Parking Management — MVP",
    "description": "Colección de regresión para los 4 endpoints del MVP.\n\nRequisitos:\n1. `docker compose up -d`\n2. `psql -f db/schema.sql` y `psql -f db/seed.sql`\n3. `npm run start:dev`\n\nCorre la colección completa con el Runner: está ordenada para que las dependencias se cumplan (crear sesión antes de consultarla, consultarla antes de cerrarla).\n\nEl seed debe estar intacto al empezar. Para volver al estado inicial:\n`docker exec -i parkingdb psql -U postgres -d ParkingDB < db/seed.sql`\n\nDos peticiones fallan hasta que `calculateAmount()` esté implementada; están marcadas con ⚠ en el nombre.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "ticketCode",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "plate",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Lots",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /lots — lista completa",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const lots = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('devuelve los 3 lots del seed', () => pm.expect(lots).to.have.lengthOf(3));",
                  "pm.test('Poniente viene marcado como inactivo', () => {",
                  "  const poniente = lots.find(l => l.name === 'Edificio Poniente');",
                  "  pm.expect(poniente.isActive).to.eql(false);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lots",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["lots"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /lots/1/availability — criterio de aceptación",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('capacity 9', () => pm.expect(body.capacity).to.eql(9));",
                  "pm.test('occupied 2', () => pm.expect(body.occupied).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.test('available 7', () => pm.expect(body.available).to.eql(7));",
                  "pm.test('los conteos son numeros, no strings', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.capacity).to.be.a('number');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.occupied).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('no expone el id del lot', () => pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('id'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lots/1/availability",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["lots", "1", "availability"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /lots/2/availability — Sur",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
